WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.075
Unit 1 is how the guide is built.

2
00:00:02.075 --> 00:00:04.312
The books already design most of this.

3
00:00:04.312 --> 00:00:08.415
Cloud Boundary and Landing Zone builds
the management group hierarchy,

4
00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:12.449
the boundary policies, the provisioning
loop, and who owns the boundary.

5
00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:17.612
Security Operations and Telemetry
chooses the posture tool on each cloud.

6
00:00:17.612 --> 00:00:22.238
Network and Transport owns the
agency's network edge and TIC.

7
00:00:22.238 --> 00:00:27.176
DNS, DHCP and IPAM owns DNS authority.

8
00:00:27.176 --> 00:00:31.525
Governance, Drift and Evidence
explains why drift is the threat.

9
00:00:31.525 --> 00:00:36.951
What none of them gives is the service-by-service
engineering of the Azure controls

10
00:00:36.951 --> 00:00:41.197
a Zero Trust assessment tests: DDoS
protection on every public I P,

11
00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:46.309
a web application firewall in prevention
mode, origins only the edge can reach,

12
00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:48.904
egress through an inspecting firewall,

13
00:00:48.904 --> 00:00:53.150
pass reachable only privately,
and keys behind role-based access.

14
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:58.320
The guide does that, in ten steps, and links
to the books instead of restating them.
